    risk_category:'High-risk AI in regulated sectors',
    effective_date:'2026-11-01', deadline:'2026-11-01',
    what_changed:'The Monetary Authority of Singapore issued a circular supplementing its Technology Risk Management Guidelines with dedicated AI governance requirements. All MAS-licensed financial institutions must from 1 November 2026: (1) maintain a Model Inventory covering all AI models in production with quarterly attestation; (2) conduct pre-deployment fairness assessments for AI models that affect credit, insurance pricing, or employment decisions; (3) implement model risk management proportionate to materiality; (4) report AI-related operational risk incidents to MAS within 72 hours; and (5) disclose AI use in customer-facing decisions on customer request.',
    previous_position:'MAS relied on general Technology Risk Management Guidelines (2021) and the voluntary Veritas Fairness Assessment Framework (2022). No mandatory AI incident reporting obligation, no Model Inventory requirement, and no mandatory fairness assessment existed. Compliance was voluntary and self-paced.',
    new_position:'Mandatory regime from 1 November 2026. Model Inventory: scope covers all production AI, quarterly attestation required. Fairness assessment: scope covers credit, insurance pricing, and employment AI; annual minimum cadence. Model risk management: Tier 1 institutions (those meeting MAS definition) must maintain a formal Model Risk Management Policy. Incident reporting: 72-hour obligation for AI operational risk incidents affecting customers or MAS-reportable systems. Customer disclosure: AI-driven decision-making must be disclosed on customer request with a human review pathway.',
    legal_significance:'Binding on all MAS-licensed financial institutions. Failure to comply constitutes a breach of technology risk management obligations enforceable under the Banking Act, Insurance Act, and Securities and Futures Act respectively. Enforcement track record: MAS issued six formal reprimands for technology risk management failures in 2025, signalling active supervisory attention.',
    business_significance:'Tier 1 banks (DBS, OCBC, UOB, Standard Chartered Singapore, HSBC Singapore, Citibank Singapore) must implement the full regime by 1 November 2026. Fintech firms with MAS Payment Institution licences face proportionate obligations scaled to their risk profile. Regional banks using Singapore as an APAC AI development hub must classify models by materiality before the November deadline and may need to implement new Model Inventory infrastructure on short timelines.',
    technical_significance:'Model Inventory must record: model purpose, owner, training data description, last evaluation date, performance metrics, fairness metrics for regulated decisions, deployment date, and retirement date. Fairness assessment must include demographic parity, equalised odds, and calibration metrics as a minimum. Incident detection requires automated monitoring for anomalous model output distributions, data drift, and API error spikes with defined alert thresholds.',
