    standfirst:'South Korea’s National Assembly passed a Personal Information Protection Act amendment on 20 August 2026 creating a dedicated statutory route to use lawfully collected personal data for AI development. The amendment is the first of its kind in South Korea, replacing reliance on time-limited regulatory sandboxes. PIPC approval is required. Effective date: six months after promulgation, which is still pending.',
    related_articles:['AR-000480','AR-000500'],
