    risk_category:'Children, education, and personal data',
    standfirst:'New York Senate Bill S10685 (Fostering Optimal Classroom Use of Screens Act) was introduced and referred to the Senate Rules Committee on 21 August 2026. The bill proposes to limit school-issued devices, prohibit generative AI, conversational AI and AI companions on those devices, require EdTech providers to register with the New York Attorney General, and restrict use of student personally identifiable information — including excluding AI model training from permitted internal business operations. It is not enacted law.',
